Device: Asus Zephyrus GA402RJ
Distro: Arch Linux
Kernel: 6.17.6

Noticed this issue after upgrading to 6.16, systems hangs when closing the =
lid of my laptop. The issue is triggered by using a distrobox container.

Steps to replicate:
1. distrobox create --pull -i docker.io/library/archlinux:latest --name tes=
t-container --home ~/Containers/test-container --additional-packages "syste=
md" --init
2. distrobox enter test-container
3. Suspend the system

Bisected to commit:
    commit 0c58a97f919c24fe4245015f4375a39ff05665b6
    Author: Joanne Koong <joannelkoong@gmail.com>
    Date:   Mon Apr 14 15:22:10 2025 -0700
   =20
        fuse: remove tmp folio for writebacks and internal rb tree

I was able to temporarily fix the issue on 6.16 by reverting 0c58a97f and 7=
d0f0f06. Unfortunately reverting 0c58a97f on 6.17 causes huge conflicts.
Attached systemd journal logs.

Regards,
Athul
